workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner
   Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End.

Description:
First, the Transportation Planner determines the primary mode of transportation and establishes the location for each day of the trip, ensuring a closed loop through two Minnesota cities. This logistical framework is then passed to the Accommodation Planner to arrange private-room lodging for 4 people. Afterwards, the plan is simultaneously passed to the Restaurant Planner and Attractions Planner, who work in parallel to find non-repeating dining and activity options specific to Minnesota cities. Once their individual plans are complete, the Final Plan Summarizer integrates all information into a comprehensive itinerary that strictly adheres to the $13,800 budget and user requirements.
